on is separate from the original filing's selected-control result.","reason":"The triggers are formalized above. The packet does not supply a performance deadline or enough guidance to decide whether an outstanding resubmission is overdue."},{"formalization":null,"name":"Registration and XML transition preparation","reading":"Firms should register accounts using the specified registration process. Firms intending XML submission must follow the separate schema and liaise with the JFIU as soon as possible to arrange a technical test. The latter wording does not itself state that a passed test is a condition precedent to every XML filing.","reason":"Registration is outside the selected control. Schema conformity is included, but intended use, liaison and the as-soon-as-possible standard require a separate temporal control."}],"shared_formalization":{"control_name":"Post-launch STR channel, submission format and electronic-certificate control","evaluation_rules":["Interpret the result only when scope is established as true.","Unknown facts remain unknown; do not replace missing evidence with false.","The web-form branch means this packet does not attach footnote 3 to that method. It does not establish an exemption from certificate requirements that might appear in unavailable materials."],"result":"(and via_streams2 (or (and is_xml_submission xml_schema_conforms submission_ecert_requirement_met) (and is_completed_prescribed_pdf_upload submission_ecert_requirement_met) is_completed_streams2_web_form))","result_type":"Boolean","scope":"(and is_licensed_firm is_str_filing at_or_after_operational_launch)","source_refs":["da12aecad4e68.u0.0","da12aecad4e68.u3.811","da12aecad4e68.u4.1003","da12aecad4e68.u5.1078","da12aecad4e68.u6.1149","da12aecad4e68.u13.2131","da12aecad4e68.u14.2439","da12aecad4e68.u30.3569"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] Within scope, true means the filing uses STREAMS 2 and one listed method, with schema conformity for XML and the footnote 3 e-Cert requirement satisfied for XML or PDF. False means at least one requirement of this selected control is not met. Neither outcome decides whole-firm compliance, STR timeliness, account registration or technical-test liaison."},"source_key":"assurance.1d77e5e08a758b5fe0a406b9","substantive_difference":{"common_ground":"Both readings require STREAMS 2 after operational launch, retain the three listed submission methods, attach footnote 3 to XML and PDF, and preserve urgent blackout contact separately.","disputed_case":"An actual STR submitted outside STREAMS 2 on 2026-02-02 before 9:00am falls outside the operational-launch resubmission trigger but inside the implementation-date trigger. A phone call or email that is only contact does not automatically count as such a submission.","relative_support":"The operational-launch reading has stronger support from the express resumption and launch times. The implementation-date reading draws support from the general effective-date clause and its footnote 2 marker.","unresolved_questions":["Does implementation in footnote 2 mean the operational launch time or the start of the stated effective date?","When does urgent blackout contact constitute actual STR submission?","Does the promised guidance require later submission of STRs communicated during any part of the blackout?","What technical act satisfies the Hongkong Post e-Cert requirement?","Which timezone governs the stated hours?"]},"task":"GENERATE","unit_accounting":[{"quote":"licensed corporations, SFC-licensed virtual asset service providers and associated entities (collectively referred to as “licensed firms”)","treatment":"Defines actor scope; the same unit introduces transition by 2026-02-02.","unit_id":"da12aecad4e68.u0.0"},{"quote":"which will replace the current STREAMS platform.","treatment":"Defines the platform transition; efficiency statements supply context, not additional selected-control conditions.","unit_id":"da12aecad4e68.u1.383"},{"quote":"STR submission","tr